/*
    Pointers are variables that referentiate a memory address, instead of
    an actual value.

    Unlike C, pointers in Quaoar are defined by adding an asterisk (*) 
    **before** the variable type.

    Addressing the memory value of variables is just like C, with an
    ampersand (&) before the variable itself.

    ```quaoar
    int value = 10
    *int pointer = &value
    *pointer = 5

    return value // value is now 5 thanks to the deref-write property of pointers!
    ```
*/
f main() int{
    int value = 5
    // int another = 10
    *int p = &value
    *p = 10

    return value // 10 if deref-write reached, 5 if it didn't
}